# Owner Excellent Standard (hard rules)

## Rule 1 — Excellent definition

**Excellent** = is point par 10 saal tak dubara developer kaam nahi — sirf chalana, keys paste, hosting.

**Open** = abhi excellent nahi.

**Never say:** mostly OK, good enough, chalega, theek hai, chhota gap, improved.

**Every audit point status:** Excellent OR Open only.

## Rule 2 — Owner override

If Owner says **Excellent** on a point → mark **Excellent** (Owner confirmed). Do not leave Open.

## Rule 3 — Multi-point batch (one chat)

When Owner sends multiple numbered points in one message:

1. Work **Point #1 first** until Excellent.
2. Do **not** start Point #2 until Point #1 is Excellent.
3. When Point #1 is Excellent → **automatically** move to Point #2 (no permission ask).
4. Repeat in order until all points done.

**Gate:** No work starts until Owner says **"continue work now"**.

## Rule 4 — Unclear = ask

If any point, chat, or instruction is unclear → tell Owner **"Ye mujhe samajh nahi aa raha"** and ask. Do not guess.

## Close report (when Excellent)

1. What was completed (code + where to click)
2. **Excellent — is point par dubara developer kaam nahi**
3. Owner manual only (keys, migration button) — not "future code work"
